   "id": "crush-functions-md-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "# Functions\n\n> Verified against crush-ast `d04bc60a` (2026-10-29).\n\nThis chapter covers defining and calling functions. Named functions are\ntop-level declarations, and they are also **values**: you can store one in a\nvariable, pass it as an argument and return it. Lambdas and closures have their\nown chapter, [Closures and Function Values](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/closures.html).\n\n## Defining functions\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn greet(name: String) {\n    print(\"Hello, \" + name + \"!\")\n}\n\nfn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {\n    return a + b\n}\n\ngreet(\"Alice\")\nprint(add(5, 3))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/functions.md:12",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "Hello, Alice!\n8\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "- Parameter and return **type hints are optional**. When present they are checked\n  at compile time at call sites (`add(\"x\", 1)` is a compile error).\n- The number of arguments is checked at compile time: `add(1)` →\n  `Function 'add' expects 2 arguments, found 1`.\n- There are no default parameter values (`fn f(x = 1)` is a parse error) and no\n  variadic parameters.\n- A function may be called before its definition appears in the file.\n\n## Returning values\n\nReturn with `return`. A function that falls off the end — or uses a bare\n`return` — yields `null`. A final expression is **not** an implicit return:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-2",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn check_sign(x: Int) -> String {\n    if x > 0 {\n        return \"positive\"\n    } else if x < 0 {\n        return \"negative\"\n    }\n    return \"zero\"\n}\n\nfn log_message(msg: String) {\n    print(\"[LOG] \" + msg)\n}\n\nprint(check_sign(5))\nprint(check_sign(-2))\nprint(check_sign(0))\nlog_message(\"done\")\nprint(log_message(\"again\"))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/functions.md:44",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "positive\nnegative\nzero\n[LOG] done\n[LOG] again\nnull\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "The return-type hint is not checked against what the body actually returns\ntoday: `fn f() -> Int { return \"s\" }` compiles.\n\n## Recursion\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int {\n    if n <= 1 {\n        return 1\n    }\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\n}\n\nfn fib(n) {\n    if n < 2 {\n        return n\n    }\n    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)\n}\n\nprint(factorial(5))\nprint(fib(15))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/functions.md:80",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "120\n610\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Mutual recursion works too. Recursion depth is capped by the VM's call-depth\nquota — **256 frames by default** (`--max-call-depth N` on `crush-run`); exceeding\nit ends the program with `call depth quota exceeded`. The other default quotas are\n1,000,000 instructions (`--max-steps`), a 4096-slot stack (`--max-stack`), 1 MiB of\noutput (`--max-output`), and a 30-second wall-clock limit per polyglot block.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-4",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn d(n) {\n    return d(n - 1)\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    print(d(1))\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
