   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-md-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "They capture variables from where they are written; that, and the rules for\ncalling function values, is in [Closures and Function Values](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/closures.html). The\nbuilt-ins `print` and `len` are not values (`let g = len` is a compile error that\nsays so, crush-ast [#257](https://github.com/nixpt/crush-ast/issues/257)); wrap them:\n`|x| len(x)`.\n\nThe pipeline operator (`x |> f`) takes a function name or a variable holding one:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-functions-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn double(n) {\n    return n * 2\n}\nfn inc(n) {\n    return n + 1\n}\nprint(5 |> double |> inc)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
